@Sanne you can cast Context to ContextInternal and use

```java

  /**
   * @return the {@link ConcurrentMap} used to store context data
   * @see Context#get(String)
   * @see Context#put(String, Object)
   */
  ConcurrentMap<Object, Object> contextData();

  /**
   * @return the {@link ConcurrentMap} used to store local context data
   */
  ConcurrentMap<Object, Object> localContextData();
```

directly, I think it works well and it allows us to not change the signature of get/put methods in Vert.x 4.1, we might consider using Object in 4.2 that would break binary compatibility but would not be a breaking change
